<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argentine Civil Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1814–1880</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Argentine Civil Wars were the series of conflicts fought from 1814 to 1880 between the Unitarians, who wanted a centralised state led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, and the Federalists, who defended provincial autonomy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a> dominated much of the period; his defeat at Caseros in 1852 led to the Constitution of 1853. Buenos Aires joined the republic after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavon">Battle of Pavón</a> (1861), and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federalism">federalisation</a> of the city in 1880 closed the conflicts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars.jpg" alt="Argentine Civil Wars" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: La_conducción_del_cadáver_de_Lavalle_en_la_quebrada_de_Humahuaca.JPG: Nicanor Blanes Batalla_de_Arroyo_Grande.jpg: Ca... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerra_Civil.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
